; Sprite: Willy facing left, walk frame 2
;
; One 16x16 sprite of 32 bytes: 16 pixel rows of 2 bytes (left byte, right byte; bit 7 = leftmost pixel), drawn with
; #R$9456. Willy walking to the left (observed: key O gives $85D0 = 3, bit 0 set), walk frame 2. #R$9637 draws Willy
; from $9D00 + 128*(bit 0 of #R$85D0) + 32*(#R$85D2 AND 3). In The Nightmare Room (room $1D) #R$9637 uses page $B6
; (#R$B600) instead.
@label=SpriteWillyLeft2
b$9DC0 DEFB $00,$F0
 $9DC2 DEFB $00,$F0
 $9DC4 DEFB $01,$F8
 $9DC6 DEFB $00,$B0
 $9DC8 DEFB $01,$F0
 $9DCA DEFB $00,$F0
 $9DCC DEFB $00,$60
 $9DCE DEFB $00,$F0
 $9DD0 DEFB $01,$D8
 $9DD2 DEFB $01,$D8
 $9DD4 DEFB $01,$D8
 $9DD6 DEFB $01,$B8
 $9DD8 DEFB $00,$F0
 $9DDA DEFB $00,$60
 $9DDC DEFB $00,$60
 $9DDE DEFB $00,$E0
